    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0055" n="43" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg43"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/12920</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-28">June 28, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister of Finland called to see me this morning at his request. The
                    Minister left with me an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi><anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d58-f1"/> giving a detailed account <pb facs="0056" n="44"
                        xml:id="pg44"/> of the hostile acts committed by Russia within Finnish
                    territory during the past few days.</p>
                <p>The Minister then read to me, by instruction of his Government, a statement of
                    the policy of the Finnish Government as already communicated by the Finnish
                    Minister in London<anchor n="3" xml:id="d58-f2"/> to the British Government. The
                    statement contained the following declaration: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Government of Finland desires to maintain unaltered its relations
                            with Great Britain. The Government of Finland is a co-belligerent with
                            Germany solely against Russia.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The Minister asked if I would make any statement as to the attitude of this
                    Government with regard to Finnish involvement in the war. I replied that I
                    should prefer to await developments for at least a few days before making any
                    such statement, but that the declaration as communicated to me by the Minister
                    would, of course, facilitate the determination which this Government would
                    reach.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
